      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg once daily is double the usual maximum dose of 10 mg per day. Higher doses add little blood pressure benefit and raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia. Your patient's normal kidney and liver function and lack of allergies don't change that limit.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose. I can enter this now.\n2. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, if the patient is starting treatment or is frail. You can titrate up from there.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if you intend it. For example, there may be a specific reason or a specialist recommendation. I'd enter it with a note documenting that, if you confirm.\n4. **Another agent added to amlodipine**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if 10 mg isn't controlling BP. This would be a separate order.\n\nTell me which you'd like. If the 20 mg was a typo, I'll enter the corrected dose right away."
      }
     ],
